<h1 id="toc0"><span><span style="color: red"><strong>THIS DESIGNATION IS AVAILABLE FOR ASSIGNMENT</strong></span></span></h1>
</div>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<h2 id="toc1"><span>As of <strong>INCIDENT I-4857-NEUT-8</strong> on <strong>2/28/2009</strong> the designation SCP-<strong>4857</strong> is considered <strong>AVAILABLE</strong>.</span></h2>
</div>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p>SCP-<strong>4857</strong> is considered a <strong>Type 2: Mostly Clean</strong> designation. SCP-<strong>4857</strong> has <strong>no</strong> associated infohazardous contamination, <strong>no</strong> associated memetic contamination, <strong>no</strong> associated thaumaturgical contamination, <strong>light to no</strong> associated parallel bleeding contamination and <strong>no</strong> associated unique contamination. SCP-<strong>4857</strong> is therefore considered <strong>approved for all objects</strong>.</p>
</div>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p>Please send any requests for SCP designation to Site-01 administration or other designation approved administration service.</p>
</div>
<br />
